# Input
```svelte
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->

{#each boxes as box}
	{@const volume = box.width * box.height * box.depth}
	<p>{volume}</p>
{/each}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.svelte:4:2 lint/nursery/noSvelteLegacyConst ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i Avoid legacy Svelte {@const} tags.
  
    3 │ {#each boxes as box}
  > 4 │ 	{@const volume = box.width * box.height * box.depth}
      │ 	^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    5 │ 	<p>{volume}</p>
    6 │ {/each}
  
  i {@const} legacy syntax is less versatile. Declaration tags are the preferred syntax for deriving values in Svelte markup.
  
  i Remove the @ and add $state() or $derived() runes if the value should be reactive, for example: {const area = $derived(box.width * box.height)}.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

